---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/sections/PageHeader.astro';
import { buildArticleSchema, buildBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const title = 'Corrugated Box Sample Approval Checklist Before Production';
const description = 'Approve corrugated box samples with checks for product fit, packed weight, closure, print, handling and documented production specifications.';
const url = '/blog/corrugated-box-sample-approval-checklist';
const image = '/images/blog/corrugated-box-sample-approval-checklist.png';
const article = buildArticleSchema({ title, description, url, datePublished: '2026-11-17', author: 'Apex Packaging Solutions', image });
const breadcrumb = buildBreadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Packaging Guides', url: '/blog' }, { name: title, url }]);
const approvalSteps = [
  ['01', 'Identity', 'Match the sample to its dieline, board, dimensions and artwork revision.'],
  ['02', 'Pack', 'Load the real product, inserts, literature and void fill.'],
  ['03', 'Measure', 'Record packed weight and outside dimensions after closure.'],
  ['04', 'Operate', 'Run erection, filling and sealing at normal packing speed.'],
  ['05', 'Inspect', 'Check print, barcode, labels, scores, seams and opening.'],
  ['06', 'Release', 'Sign the exact sample and production specification.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} image={image} schemaBlocks={[breadcrumb, article]}>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Corrugated box quality" heading={title} lead="Approve the packed system, production specification and acceptance record, not just an empty sample that looks correct." imageSrc={image} imageAlt="Fictional Nova Supply corrugated samples, board swatches and measuring tools arranged for packaging approval" />
  <main>
    <section class="intro-band"><div class="article-shell intro-grid">
      <div><p class="article-meta">FIELD GUIDE · NOVEMBER 17, 2026 · 7 MIN READ</p><p class="standfirst">A sample is the last inexpensive place to find a packaging mistake. The approval must represent how the box will be erected, packed, sealed, handled and identified in production.</p></div>
      <aside class="decision-note"><p class="note-label">THE APPROVAL RULE</p><p>Approve a named revision with a known packout. An attractive empty box is not evidence that the shipping system works.</p></aside>
    </div></section>

    <section class="steps-band" aria-labelledby="approval-path"><div class="article-shell">
      <p class="section-kicker">THE APPROVAL PATH</p><h2 id="approval-path">Six gates before production release</h2>
      <div class="step-grid">{approvalSteps.map(([number, label, copy]) => <div class="step-item"><span>{number}</span><h3>{label}</h3><p>{copy}</p></div>)}</div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="editorial-section"><div class="article-shell split-layout">
      <div class="article-copy"><p class="section-kicker">GATE 01–02 · IDENTITY + FIT</p><h2>Make the sample traceable, then pack the real configuration</h2>
        <p>Label the sample with the supplier, date, dieline or style reference, inside dimensions, board construction and artwork revision. State whether it is a plain structural sample, a digital mock-up or a production-equivalent sample. A white sample can prove fit, but not necessarily production colour, coating, scoring or registration.</p>
        <p>Load production-representative products, inserts, bags, literature and void fill. When one box serves several SKUs, test the largest, smallest and heaviest configurations. The product should load without forcing the walls and remain controlled when the closed box is turned through every orientation.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/services/corrugated-boxes">Review corrugated box options →</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="article-figure"><img src="/images/blog/corrugated-sample-fit-check.png" alt="Fictional Northfield Labs corrugated mailer sample undergoing product-fit inspection" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Fit approval uses the intended product, insert and pack orientation—not an empty carton.</figcaption></figure>
    </div></section>

    <section class="calculation-band"><div class="article-shell calculation-grid">
      <div><p class="section-kicker light">GATE 03 · PACKED WEIGHT</p><h2>Test the shipment you will actually send</h2><p>Use the intended tape width and pattern, adhesive, staples or locking features. Then measure and weigh the fully closed package. Reopening a test box changes its condition; use a fresh sample for subsequent handling checks.</p></div>
      <div class="weight-example" aria-label="Packed weight example"><div><span>12 units</span><strong>× 0.75 kg</strong></div><div><span>Products</span><strong>9.0 kg</strong></div><div><span>Box + insert</span><strong>+ 0.8 kg</strong></div><div class="weight-total"><span>Test weight</span><strong>9.8 kg</strong></div></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="editorial-section muted-section"><div class="article-shell split-layout reverse-layout">
      <figure class="article-figure"><img src="/images/blog/corrugated-print-barcode-approval.png" alt="Fictional Meridian Goods corrugated box undergoing barcode, print and closure inspection" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Scan the final barcode position on a packed, closed box under representative conditions.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="article-copy"><p class="section-kicker">GATE 04–05 · PACKOUT + PRINT</p><h2>Run the line, close the box and inspect every panel</h2>
        <p>Ask the people who will use the packaging to erect, fill and seal it at normal speed. Watch for slow locks, awkward hand movements, flap gaps, bulging and inconsistent tape placement. A structure that works only when handled delicately is not production-ready.</p>
        <p>Compare every printed panel with the controlled artwork. Confirm orientation, legal copy, product codes, colour reference and version marks. Scores, the manufacturer’s joint and tape must not hide important information. Visual sharpness is not barcode verification.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/blog/packaging-artwork-requirements-bleed-dielines-barcodes-ink-limits">Use the packaging artwork checklist →</a>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="route-band"><div class="article-shell route-layout">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">GATE 05 · DISTRIBUTION</p><h2>Match the handling check to the route</h2><p>Document whether the package moves through parcel, palletized LTL, warehouse transfer or retail replenishment. Then agree a test plan around the real hazards, product fragility and acceptance criteria. Informal drops may reveal obvious weakness, but they do not replace controlled validation.</p><p><a href="https://store.astm.org/standards/d4169">ASTM D4169</a> provides a framework for evaluating sequential distribution hazards. <a href="https://ista.org/getting_started_with_design.php">ISTA packaged-product testing</a> supports design decisions; ISTA 3A addresses parcel-delivery shipments up to 70 kg (150 lb). The correct procedure depends on the route and objective—one result is not a universal guarantee.</p></div>
      <div class="route-list"><div><span>PARCEL</span><p>Drop, vibration, compression and closure integrity.</p></div><div><span>LTL / PALLET</span><p>Stacking, pallet pattern, overhang and containment.</p></div><div><span>RETAIL</span><p>Case opening, replenishment, labels and shelf presentation.</p></div></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="signoff-band"><div class="article-shell signoff-grid">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">GATE 06 · RELEASE</p><h2>The production sign-off</h2><p>A useful approval record makes the decision reproducible. Photograph the empty and packed sample, all six panels, closure and label positions. List deviations and state whether each requires a revised sample or a controlled production correction.</p></div>
      <div class="checklist" role="list" aria-label="Production approval checklist"><p role="listitem">Sample ID matches the specification and artwork revision.</p><p role="listitem">Contents, pack arrangement, dimensions and weight are recorded.</p><p role="listitem">Fit, movement, opening and normal-speed packout are approved.</p><p role="listitem">Closure material, pattern, labels and barcode are approved.</p><p role="listitem">Route-specific test method and acceptance criteria are agreed.</p><p role="listitem">Approver, date and every authorized exception are signed.</p></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="cta-band"><div class="article-shell cta-layout"><div><p class="section-kicker light">READY TO SAMPLE</p><h2>Turn the approval into a controlled production brief</h2><p>Reference the exact sample, specification and artwork revision. Apex Packaging Solutions supports Canadian and US buyers with corrugated structure, sampling, print and production coordination.</p></div><a href="/contact">Discuss your box project <span>→</span></a></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article-shell{width:min(1180px,calc(100% - 40px));margin-inline:auto}.intro-band,.editorial-section,.route-band,.signoff-band{padding:72px 0}.intro-grid,.split-layout,.calculation-grid,.route-layout,.signoff-grid,.cta-layout{display:grid;gap:48px}.intro-grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.35fr) minmax(280px,.65fr);align-items:start}.article-meta,.section-kicker,.note-label{margin:0 0 16px;color:#a97700;font-size:.76rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em}.standfirst{margin:0;max-width:780px;font-size:1.5rem;line-height:1.55;color:#292725}.decision-note{border-left:4px solid #c89200;padding:8px 0 8px 26px}.decision-note p:last-child{margin:0;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.65;color:#3f3b36}.steps-band{padding:64px 0;background:#111;color:#fff}.steps-band h2,.calculation-band h2,.cta-band h2{margin:0;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:0}.step-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));margin-top:42px;border-top:1px solid #444;border-left:1px solid #444}.step-item{min-height:190px;padding:26px;border-right:1px solid #444;border-bottom:1px solid #444}.step-item span{color:#d5a000;font-weight:800}.step-item h3{margin:30px 0 8px;font-size:1.15rem}.step-item p{margin:0;color:#c8c5bf;line-height:1.55}.split-layout{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.84fr) minmax(440px,1.16fr);align-items:center}.article-copy h2,.route-layout h2,.signoff-grid h2{margin:0 0 24px;font-size:clamp(2rem,3.7vw,3.25rem);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:0}.article-copy p,.route-layout>div>p,.signoff-grid>div>p{color:#4a4641;font-size:1.06rem;line-height:1.78}.article-figure{margin:0;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid #ded8cf;background:#fff}.article-figure img{display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;object-fit:cover}.article-figure figcaption{padding:14px 18px;color:#68615a;font-size:.86rem;line-height:1.5}.text-link{display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;color:#936b00;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}.calculation-band{padding:72px 0;background:#b68500;color:#fff}.calculation-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr minmax(360px,.7fr);align-items:center}.calculation-band p{max-width:670px;color:#fff9e8;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75}.light{color:#fff3c4}.weight-example{border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.5)}.weight-example div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;padding:16px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.35)}.weight-example div:last-child{border-bottom:0}.weight-example span{color:#fff5d7}.weight-example strong{font-size:1.08rem}.weight-total{background:#111}.muted-section{background:#f3f1ed}.reverse-layout{grid-template-columns:minmax(440px,1.16fr) minmax(0,.84fr)}.route-layout{grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;align-items:start}.route-list{border-top:3px solid #111}.route-list div{padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d7d1c8}.route-list span{font-size:.75rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#a97700}.route-list p{margin:8px 0 0;color:#494540}.signoff-band{background:#faf8f4}.signoff-grid{grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;align-items:start}.checklist{border-top:3px solid #c89200}.checklist p{position:relative;margin:0;padding:17px 16px 17px 42px;border-bottom:1px solid #d9d4cb;color:#302d29}.checklist p::before{content:'✓';position:absolute;left:12px;color:#a97700;font-weight:900}.cta-band{padding:64px 0;background:#111;color:#fff}.cta-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr auto;align-items:center}.cta-band p{max-width:760px;color:#c8c5bf;line-height:1.7}.cta-layout>a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;padding:16px 22px;background:#c89200;color:#111;font-weight:900;text-decoration:none}.cta-layout>a span{font-size:1.4rem}@media(max-width:900px){.intro-grid,.split-layout,.calculation-grid,.route-layout,.signoff-grid,.cta-layout,.reverse-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.step-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.article-figure{order:2}.cta-layout>a{justify-self:start}}@media(max-width:560px){.article-shell{width:min(100% - 28px,1180px)}.intro-band,.editorial-section,.route-band,.signoff-band,.calculation-band{padding:48px 0}.standfirst{font-size:1.25rem}.step-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.step-item{min-height:auto}.split-layout{gap:30px}.article-copy h2,.route-layout h2,.signoff-grid h2,.steps-band h2,.calculation-band h2,.cta-band h2{font-size:2rem}.weight-example div{padding:14px}.cta-layout>a{width:100%;justify-content:space-between}}
  .steps-band h2,.calculation-band h2,.cta-band h2,.step-item h3{color:#fff}
</style>
